A||N||3||gtcash||V8 Conversion Headers?||||5||
Z||000000||gtcash||04-30-2001||12:34 AM||||I have an old conversion 350 Chev, 84 Coupe, 2 into 1 muffler and exhaust...<BR>I want duals! With less back pressure...<BR>What's available?<BR>Mufflers can be loud, I don't have to worry about emissions...Not as loud as my motorcycle, please...<BR>Headers? Or what manifolds work best and fit?<BR>I posted this question on Archie's site days ago and no replys...what's up?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||04-30-2001||12:53 AM||||I believe archie uses the Ram horn GM maifolds for economy installs , or for higher dollar stuff the Sanderson block hugger headers , they look like there made for the conversion. USe the esearch function and look up v8 headers , there are a bunch of pics floating around<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||04-30-2001||10:26 AM||||Hi GTCASH!<P>Welcome to the forum! I think the headers that I told you on our last meeting was one of these two. A call to Archie would give you the right part number.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.sandersonheaders.com/pagesbypartnum/cc1ap.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sandersonheaders.com/pagesbypartnum/cc1ap.htm</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.sandersonheaders.com/pagesbypartnum/qp1000a.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sandersonheaders.com/pagesbypartnum/qp1000a.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||04-30-2001||12:53 PM||||If you want to use a header, use this one <A HREF="http://www.sandersonheaders.com/pagesbypartnum/cc90.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sandersonheaders.com/pagesbypartnum/cc90.htm</A> <P>Otherwise use the "Ram-Horn" style exhaust manifolds.<P>Archie<P>The "Ram Horns" look like this <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-134s.jpg"> <P>The cc90's look like this<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-325s.jpg"> ||||reg||1
